; Per-head positional counts — the `(head :name … :min … :max …)` spelling
; of `:heads`.
;
; A head-set says *which* heads a slot accepts. On a form's `:positional`
; slot — the one place a head has a repeated population — it can also say
; *how many*. The compact `:names [a b c]` spelling cannot: the two
; spellings are mutually exclusive, so declaring one bound means writing
; every head as a `(head …)` child.
;
; Three bounds appear below, and the floor defaulting to 0 is the thing to
; read carefully:
;
;   :min 1 :max 1   exactly one
;   :max 1          at most one — none is fine
;   (no bound)      any number, including none
;
; Two shapes here exist to pin what the counts *don't* do:
;
;   * `(section-holder :section …)` reuses `pipeline-section` on a KEYED
;     slot, where the bounds are inert — a keyed slot holds one value, so
;     `:max 1` is trivially satisfied and `:min 1` has no set to be
;     missing from. Inert rather than rejected, so a bounded kind stays
;     shareable between a slot with a population and one without.
;   * `(scratch-pipeline …)` is `:open true` with the same bounded slot.
;     Openness widens the *keyword* surface; it does not turn the counts
;     off. A form that declares `:positional <bounded-kind>` opted in.
;
; Export side: JSON Schema renders the counts as one `contains` +
; `minContains` / `maxContains` per bounded head, in the `$children`
; array's `allOf` beside the whole-set `items` union. Not
; `minItems`/`maxItems` — those bound the array's total length, which says
; nothing about how many children carry any one head. TypeScript cannot
; express a per-member array count at all, so the `.d.ts` carries the
; bounds as a doc comment and nothing more.
(plugin :name head-counts :version "1.0.0"
  :description "Reference plugin for per-head positional counts on a head-set."

  (form :name vertex
    :description "The vertex stage of a pipeline."
    (key :name entry :type symbol :optional false))

  (form :name fragment
    :description "The fragment stage. Optional — a depth-only pass has none."
    (key :name entry :type symbol :optional false))

  (form :name constant
    :description "A pipeline-overridable constant. Any number of these."
    (key :name name  :type symbol :optional false)
    (key :name value :type number :optional false))

  (value-kind :name pipeline-section
    :description "One section of a render pipeline, with how many of each are allowed."
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set
      (head :name vertex   :min 1 :max 1 :description "The vertex stage. Exactly one.")
      (head :name fragment :max 1        :description "The fragment stage. At most one.")
      (head :name constant               :description "Pipeline-overridable constant. Any number.")))

  (form :name render-pipeline
    :description "A pipeline whose sections are counted, not just typed."
    :positional pipeline-section
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false))

  (form :name section-holder
    :description "Same kind, keyed slot — the counts ride along inertly here."
    (key :name section :type pipeline-section :optional true))

  (form :name scratch-pipeline
    :description "Open form, same bounded slot: `:open true` does not silence the counts."
    :open true
    :positional pipeline-section))
